<title>USA: Mark IV Industries Q1 May 31 net increases.</title>
<headline>Mark IV Industries Q1 May 31 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>AMHERST, N.Y. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997		1996</p>
<p> Sales from continuing operations    $560,100	  $540,900</p>
<p> Operating income			    63,600	    59,700</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations     30,100	    27,300</p>
<p> Income from discontinued operations	  -	     1,200</p>
<p> Net income				    30,100	    28,500</p>
<p>Primary earnings per share:</p>
<p>    Continuing operations		    0.46		0.41</p>
<p>    Discontinued operations		     -		0.02</p>
<p>	Net income				 0.46		0.43</p>
<p>Fully-diluted earnings per share:</p>
<p>    Continuing operations		    0.46		0.41</p>
<p>    Discontinued operations		     -		0.02</p>
<p>	Net income				 0.46		0.43</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>shares outstanding:</p>
<p>    Primary				    65,600	    66,300</p>
<p>    Fully-diluted			    66,000	    66,700</p>
<p>	  (Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Oper income is income from continuing operations before interest expense and taxes.</p>
<p>As a result of share repurchases of 2.6 million shares, fully-diluted weighted average shares outstanding declined slightly to 66 million from 66.7 million.</p>
<p>All share and share-related amounts have been restated to reflect five percent stock dividend distributed in May 1997.</p>
<p>Fiscal 1997 results reflect divested businesses as discontinued operations, and 1996 quarterly results have been restated to reflect this treatment.</p>
</text>
